# Bounce on OpenFL

The assemblage is the ball against a wall — same model as `bounce.wcn`. Target is OpenFL with P5-style `init` / `step` in Haxe: `init` builds the heap, `step` asks Game to step then draws. The compiler only wires those two functions onto a Sprite frame loop.

For the same window driven by `$Time` (Target ticks the clock, Game reacts), see `bounce_openfl_time.wcn`.

## Schema

```
Game = PlayArea Ball
PlayArea = Rect
Rect = Int/x Int/y Int/width Int/height
Ball = Int/x Int/y Int/dx Int/dy Int/rad
```

## Construction

```
[:Game
  [:PlayArea [0 0 800 600]]
  [:Ball 200 150 6 5 16]
]
```

## Methods

```
Game::bounceDx = {
  r = playArea.rect.
  if ((ball.x < r.x) or (ball.x > (r.x + r.width))) { -ball.dx } else { ball.dx }
}

Game::bounceDy = {
  r = playArea.rect.
  if ((ball.y < r.y) or (ball.y > (r.y + r.height))) { -ball.dy } else { ball.dy }
}

Game::step = {
  ndx = this.bounceDx().
  ndy = this.bounceDy().
  [:Game playArea [:Ball (ball.x + ndx) (ball.y + ndy) ndx ndy ball.rad]]
}
```

## Target

```
%openfl

%init
var assemblage:Game;

function init():Void {
    assemblage = gameFactory();
}

%step
function step():Void {
    assemblage = assemblage.step();
    var r = assemblage.playArea.rect;
    var b = assemblage.ball;
    graphics.clear();
    graphics.beginFill(0x2a2a2a);
    graphics.drawRect(r.x, r.y, r.width, r.height);
    graphics.endFill();
    graphics.beginFill(0xf2f2f2);
    graphics.drawCircle(b.x, b.y, b.rad);
    graphics.endFill();
}
```
